From 13262367e6ece45f66c2f3810fb2f4fba05b2509 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mup-2388 <288946382+mup-2388@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:16:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix screen vision crash, offline HUD fallback, and bar error
 surfacing

- llm_providers.vision(): accept a plain string OR a list of OpenAI-style
  messages and flatten it before .strip(), so a caller can never trip over
  "'list' object has no attribute 'strip'". screen.describe() now passes the
  prompt string directly instead of a message list.
- static/arc_reactor.js: Three.js loads via a guarded dynamic import and the
  whole WebGL scene builds behind an `if (THREE)` guard, with null checks on
  the renderer and setAnimationLoop. An offline laptop or a WebGL-blocklisted
  GPU now degrades to the CSS HUD (terminal, telemetry, mic, TTS) instead of
  killing the entire module at startup.
- static/arc_reactor.js: attachPlaybackAnalyser no longer double-connects the
  media element into the gain node when the mic analyser is not yet present.
- static/bar.js: formatAnswer surfaces payload.error/payload.message so a
  failed command explains itself rather than showing a bare "Failed.".

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
